WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.249
No social critic is more withering

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.439
toward identity politics and cancel

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.149
culture than the playwright and

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:07.829
comedian Andrew Doyle.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.209
Whether it's creating Titania

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:11.249
McGrath, the Twitter parody

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.529
of a woke twentysomething poet,

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:15.359
or penning a bestselling defense of

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.439
free speech.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.569
The Oxford educated and openly

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:20.429
gay Doyle never misses

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.889
an opportunity to show the folly

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.509
of political correctness.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.159
He sat down with Reason to talk

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.989
about his forthcoming book, The

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.239
New Puritans How the Religion

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.519
of Social Justice Captured

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:33.690
the Western World.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:38.599
Andrew Doyle, it's good to be

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:39.539
talking to you again.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.299
Thanks for talking to Reason.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.199
Thanks for having me.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.200
Nice to see you.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.499
Let's you know, we've we've talked a

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:47.159
couple times over the past few years

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.979
on similar although, you

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.959
know, disparate themes, but they

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.209
all revolve around kind of

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.339
wokeness, political correctness,

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:57.319
conformity as the

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.749
enemy of the good society,

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:01.729
of critical thinking, of

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:03.469
of anything that approaches

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:04.789
progress.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.039
The new book, which is

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.779
I'll just say, editorialized at the

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.309
beginning, is a phenomenal read.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.469
It's a learned read that

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:14.659
is, you know, it

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.279
makes it's creamed spinach.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:18.439
It tastes delicious while

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.319
also giving you fiber and

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.219
and much needed minerals and

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:24.079
vitamins. So it's the new

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:26.119
Puritans have the religion

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:27.979
of social justice captured

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:29.689
the western world.

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:31.879
What is the

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:33.619
elevator pitch?

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:35.569
So you are with one of

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:37.429
your heroes, Roald Dahl, in

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.739
the glass elevator

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:41.719
that shows up at Charlie

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:43.489
and the Chocolate Factory.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:45.429
What do you define the book,

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:45.889
quickly in an elevator pitch.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.509
I mean, in an elevator pitch, it's a

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:48.889
fact. I mean, I suppose the pitch

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:50.329
relates to the reasons why I wrote

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:52.489
the book. And I think we are

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:54.379
at a stage now in this culture

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.299
war or whatever we want to call it,

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.980
where many, many people are baffled.

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:00.739
They you know, there's this movement

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.089
that is sort of seize control of all

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:03.529
of our major institutions, be they

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:04.907
political or academic or the media

00:02:04.908 --> 00:02:06.739
over in the UK, the

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:09.049
NHS even, the army, the judiciary,

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:11.449
absolutely everywhere seized power

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:12.769
and control in a way that the

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:13.939
political correctness movement of

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:15.349
the eighties and nineties never did.

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:16.639
And this is the major distinction

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:17.640
between the two.

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:20.329
And yet the movement and we can see

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:22.219
most people can sort of see

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.319
that this ideology has

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.389
regressive elements, is taking

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:28.399
us back, taking us to some very dark

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:29.989
places, that it is a illiberal, that

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:31.939
it is divisive, all the rest

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:33.949
of it. And yet people are confused

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:35.569
because it uses language that

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:36.859
describes itself in the opposite

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:37.819
terms.

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:39.409
So it is a movement that is grounded

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:40.969
in what they call social justice,

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:42.889
and yet it works against true

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.329
social justice.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.339
It uses phrases like anti-racist,

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:47.989
which of course everyone wants to

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:49.039
get on board with because we're all

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.119
opposed to racism.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:51.919
And yet people can see that, oh,

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.759
hang on a minute. Suddenly we have

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.189
people, schools, segregating

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:57.019
children by skin color

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:58.669
in the name of this anti-racism.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.419
What's all that about?

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:02.539
It uses words like equity and people

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:03.709
think that sounds great as well

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:04.699
because they think it's the same as

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:05.700
equality.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:07.939
It calls itself progressive when it

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:09.229
is regressive, it calls itself

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:11.059
liberal when it is illiberal.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.189
So ultimately,

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:14.989
the more I've read and thought about

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:16.129
this, the more I realized that the

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:17.419
culture war of the present is really

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:18.859
a battle about language and who gets

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:20.989
to control definitions of words.

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:23.179
And so in order to combat it,

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:25.009
there's an extra shield, if you

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.269
like. You know, you can't just

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:27.949
challenge the ideas that are being

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:29.809
presented in the way that in a

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.849
traditional method,

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:33.679
through the Socratic method or

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.389
through traditional evidence led and

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.339
enlightenment values, because this

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:40.129
movement has is impervious

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:42.199
to reason and that is a deliberate

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.279
aspect to it.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.309
And also, its

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:46.839
practitioners have the habit of

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:48.879
redefining language

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:49.960
so that you end up,

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.069
they can basically dance around the

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:56.259
salvoes of their critics because

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:57.849
when you try and criticize them,

00:03:57.850 --> 00:03:58.989
they say, Yeah, but the words you're

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:00.939
using to criticize us

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.559
don't mean the things you think they

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:03.560
mean.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.159
So the book has been

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:07.509
written hopefully to make all this

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:08.439
accessible.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:10.059
In other words, I'm using a number

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:11.259
of analogies.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:12.579
I call it the religion of social

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:14.259
justice. I think using the analogy

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:15.549
of religion is very a very

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:17.648
accessible way to make sense

00:04:17.649 --> 00:04:18.429
of this.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:20.439
For most people I'm comparing it to,

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:23.259
I call them the New Puritans because

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:24.459
I believe it is a kind of purity

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:25.269
culture.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:26.979
It's a culture that has expectations

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:28.959
of moral purity in

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:30.969
line with what

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.499
these ideologues believe to be

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:33.529
morally pure.

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:34.530
I have to sort of caveat that

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.119
so I'm using those analogies, I'm

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:38.229
talking through the various

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:40.059
language, the origins of the

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:42.069
movement, where it's come from, how

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:43.070
it sees control.

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:46.599
I give innumerable

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.239
examples of where you seize control.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:50.769
You know, when people say there is

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:52.269
no culture war, it's a right-wing

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:54.279
myth. Well, I've layered example

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:56.679
upon example in the footnotes.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:58.999
And I should have you point out

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.239
are you are not a man of the right.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.410
No. No, I'm not.

